      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "You need to clarify between world and instance here.\nBecause If you mean instance, then I agree, that shouldn't be possible.\nBut if you mean world, then no I disagree. Being the uploader of a world shouldn't give an individual the right to go around acting like they're in charge of every instance of it. Same as how creators don't get the right to barge into any private instance.\nIf a world creator does something that is enough to result in the majority of people there wanting rid of them, then they should be removed same as anyone else. Their right to be in their own creation has not been taken away, they can still create their own instances or go to any other.\nIf an uploader wants total control of a space, then that's what uploading as private is for. Perhaps in future the groups system will allow a designated collection of people to \"own\" a world, and use it in this manner.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
