      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{60a61b373332241d8a817fb7|full_name}:\n\nNowadays we are mainly using Group Public instances anyway. There we can definitely choose to not allow the world's creator to enter. And in some cases we are forced to do it, if the world's creator is trying to impose their will on other groups' instances.\n\nIf the world's creator is targeting people out of pure malice, and they complain about those people using their world even in private. Then having them de-publish the world is the only way to give them their way. More world privacy options would be a great alternative.\n\nSad to say, but some world creators are just crazy. And given that they have moderation powers in ALL instances of their world, clearly makes them feel entitled to act however they please.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
