      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{60a61b373332241d8a817fb7|full_name}:\n\nMaking the world creator immune to punishment would put them above the rules of the instance owner (group in a group instances, or person in private instances). Basically allowing the world creator to ignore the rules if they so please, and the instance owner can do nothing to them.\n\nSince the world creator does have said moderation powers, they also have the power to even more do as they please. This means that instance owner can be kicked from the instance if the world creator don't like them.\n\nI would agree and say that players with moderation powers in an instance should be immune to being kicked. But then the world creator needs to not have said moderation powers while they aren't the instance owner.\n\nThe world creator currently being the instance owner of all normal public instances should be more than a good enough \"nod\" to their effort. And there it doesn't compromise the power if any other instance owners.",
